    refactor(shiploop): use one current receipt format for R08
    
    Owner-directed roll-forward simplification
    
    The owner clarified that no backward-compatible execution format is needed:
    "Any formats, just roll forward. Keep it in a simple format." Replace the
    unmerged b16de3c82bca456ce0a15c0c120d1935b81c50f0 candidate's separate
    JUDGEMENT_VERSION/judgement_version with the existing schema, now
    shiploop-test-loop/v2. This is an explicit change of direction from the
    parent's earlier v1-preservation choice, not evidence that compatibility
    was required.
    
    Candidate and both check/numbered Proof reuse require the current SCHEMA.
    Whole-answer keys bind test_schema to that same constant. Existing producers
    already write the schema. Missing/v1 receipt schemas or whole-answer keys
    cause current execution; there is no migration, conversion or rejudgment of
    stored output tails. Current v2 passes still reuse. The pytest error tally fix
    from the preceding commit remains: errors fail the run without inflating ran.
    
    The fidelity report reader recognizes emitted v2 records beside the archived
    v1 records it already measured. This is counts/presence reporting, not an
    execution acceptance fallback. No frozen run artifact is rewritten or
    regraded, and no adapter is added. Active synthetic fixtures use v2; the
    historical Run Review excerpt stays v1. Remove the newly introduced
    historical-v1 floor promise/test; existing floor readers and checks remain.
    
    Evidence and review follow-through
    
    A fresh Sol 6.1 medium worker used explicit shiploop profile and model/effort
    controls. All 18 selected methods pass, with stable source hashes across both
    green runs. They cover the eight parser/judge/reuse R08 methods, the new
    actual-v2-producer-to-fidelity check, existing unknown-format/zero-count
    reporting controls, analysis/delta/handoff consumers and release reporting.
    The no-ID base judge now has direct mixed-error and clean-pass controls,
    closing the prior Astra review's nonblocking suggestion. Regression and
    earlier-step base rows remain counted, with error counts excluded from ran.
    The whole-answer test explicitly verifies all non-test_schema key fields
    remain equal.
    
    The roll-forward red run is retained with an incomplete overall identity:
    an unselected historical Run Review fixture was restored during execution.
    Selected runtime/test files were stable; do not call that snapshot fully
    stable. Both final green snapshots are stable. The original pre-fix red
    evidence (20 assertion failures, zero fixture errors after correcting its
    fixture) remains unchanged and separately revision-pinned.
    
    The earlier 28-suite quick run was cancelled on the owner's design change:
    four suites completed successfully, no observed failure, source HEAD/status
    and 5,590 hashes unchanged. Its result is INCOMPLETE/superseded, not final
    acceptance. It was stopped after 718.46 seconds, and no recorded process
    survived. Final integrated verification and independent review are pending.
    
    Relevant decisions and next integration
    
    Read full relevant messages, including 57afe99d28c6a1f965d29853f09850828561557b
    and 9ce5f8a37ce22cdd1fff27a0e5860630e35811e9: report receipt discovery accurately
    and keep original evidence frozen. Earlier masked-failure and reuse decisions
    cited in b16de3c remain, with the owner's current-format boundary.
    
    Main advanced during this work with 92b55c8033c3e4f38aa137db47df05c4a8796a37
    and 44bb06a1dca281edee3856a1c6b9d9d05f193763 (TAP reader), plus
    830a38f26b9b44b4f74781a2030dc017d0cc82ee (measurement reader). Their full
    messages and review/learning commits were read. Integrate that release before
    final acceptance; its old-reader reuse fixture needs the newly authorized
    v1-to-v2 refusal expectation. Do not alter the frozen TAP replay findings.
    
