commit 36b57feb4cd0f24be00e6326db692a6bb4f6cf2a
Author:     Jim Wiese <dadleet@BigDog.local>
AuthorDate: Sun Nov 15 08:00:26 2026 -0800
Commit:     Jim Wiese <dadleet@BigDog.local>
CommitDate: Sun Nov 15 09:09:08 2026 -0800

    fix(shiploop): reject pytest errors and invalidate obsolete passed receipts
    
    Owner-authorized R08 implementation
    
    The owner approved implementing R08 first, with regression tests for mixed
    pass/error results and stale receipt reuse, keeping the solution generic and
    simple. This candidate changes three existing runtime files, two existing test
    modules and one patch note. No prompt text, product-specific rules, loop limits,
    external-state freshness policy or release output changes.
    
    Why this change and which earlier decisions hold
    
    The re-anchored audit 2a6514d6219a60bea080b4114f3e3433eec0f774 reproduced exit zero
    plus '1 passed, 1 error' passing at the shared judge, and obsolete passed
    candidate/Proof receipts being reused on an unchanged tree. The pytest reader
    already recognized the error token but omitted it from both tallies.
    
    Read full relevant messages before editing. 5fb2978401b12278839670a9e1024a478989518e
    made reporter-recognized failures authoritative over a masked zero exit.
    b446994cfbf3ad40c08cfa4ed6b926213175623e applied that decision to the no-ID base
    judge. a3b2f975487ebb7ede6987628c4a931941f9b057 adopted D5 reuse to avoid redundant
    commands while reapplying count floors. 5086baf688a611172003e0fac4417dba06bb4e0c
    added the whole-answer shortcut and deliberately retained lower-level reuse.
    Preserve all four decisions: fix incorrect verdicts without removing valid reuse
    or historical floor evidence.
    
    Implementation and compatibility decision
    
    The pytest reader adds singular/plural summary errors to failed only, after the
    existing ran calculation. A setup/collection error cannot establish another
    executed test or inflate its count floor. Existing judge refusal precedence is
    unchanged, including no-tests, minimum count and missing ID controls.
    
    One JUDGEMENT_VERSION constant and script-written judgement_version marker bind
    candidate/Proof reuse and the whole-answer key. Missing or older markers cause
    current command execution; compatible passes still reuse with provenance.
    Both check and numbered Proof receipts are covered. No saved history is erased,
    no run-state migration is needed, and no truncated output tail is rejudged.
    
    A fresh read-only gpt-6-astra/high review confirmed the affected reuse paths,
    count semantics and acceptance matrix. Parent adopted that advice but changed
    its proposed receipt-schema bump: test/shiploop_e2e/fidelity.py explicitly reads
    shiploop-test-loop/v1, so a v2 format label would make unchanged-format evidence
    unread by an existing consumer. Keep SCHEMA v1 and use one judgment marker;
    no new version registry or module. Actual requested launch controls and the
    successful review exit are retained; server-served identity is not claimed.
    
    Fail-first evidence and current candidate checks
    
    The Sol 6.1 medium worker first added regressions while all three production
    files matched 2a6514d6219a60bea080b4114f3e3433eec0f774 byte for byte. The corrected
    red runs produced 20 assertion failures and zero fixture errors over seven
    methods; the historical floor control passed. An earlier whole-answer fixture
    reset error is retained separately and is not counted as defect evidence.
    
    After the fix, all nine new methods passed: two parser/judge methods plus seven
    callback/reuse/floor methods. Cases cover singular/plural errors, exit 0 and 1,
    unchanged executed counts, passing FAILED titles, refused mixed output in three
    suite kinds and the actual step-Proof callback, old/missing markers on candidate
    and check/numbered Proof receipts, a whole-answer legacy yes with unchanged
    package/tree/draft/state, unchanged acceptance state after refusal, preserved
    historical files/floors, and current compatible lower-level reuse. Existing
    whole-answer no-rerun controls remain for the broader suite. git diff --check
    passed. The established quick bank and independent final diff review are still
    pending; this candidate remains on its isolated branch until those complete.
    
    Evidence location
    
    /Users/dadleet/.codex/visualizations/2026/10/18/01a14c60-cd70-7921-b457-5cf870234201/r08-20261115/
    contains worker/outcomes.json, raw red/green stdout/stderr, fail-first source
    hashes, final source hashes, launch controls, plan advice and parent decision.
    The plan/evidence update will retain those results after broader verification.
    
    Limits
    
    This fixes the deterministic R08 defects; it does not establish external target
    freshness (R21), reinterpret retry-to-pass output, migrate historical acceptance,
    or certify live delivery. A future judge/count semantic change must bump the
    single judgment version. No live model delivery, platform deployment, release,
    full repository suite or new CI is claimed by this candidate commit.
    
    No-E2E-Round: scoped deterministic verdict and receipt-compatibility fix with fail-first callback regressions; no prompt, host or live-delivery change.
    Co-Authored-By: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
